WEBVTT

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:25.500
I see.

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:30.460
If you're able to speak English that well, I see a future for you as our country's UN ambassador.

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:35.130
Stop that, Papa. I'm not even interested in politics.

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:36.390
Is that right?

00:00:38.510 --> 00:00:39.560
Here.

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:40.350
Thank you.

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:52.070
Hmm... understood.

00:00:53.530 --> 00:00:55.780
Argh... forgive me.

00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:59.200
Something has come up that I must take care of.

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:00.620
Really?

00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:09.340
Oh.

00:01:09.340 --> 00:01:12.880
Can you call a taxi once they've finished with their food?

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:14.420
Of course, sir.

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:18.550
Thank you very much.

00:01:35.190 --> 00:01:37.530
Are you sure you want to leave your family alone?

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:40.030
Country first, right?

00:01:40.030 --> 00:01:43.660
Does that mean our physical intercourse takes the back seat?

00:01:43.660 --> 00:01:45.750
Oh, that also comes first.

00:01:46.830 --> 00:01:50.630
This is Undersecretary Ferguson's staff list and a rough sketch of his office.

00:01:50.630 --> 00:01:56.090
What we need to know now is who he's going to negotiate with next and where.

00:01:56.090 --> 00:01:58.970
Shop talk? That's curt of you.

00:01:58.970 --> 00:02:01.300
You'll get your "bonus" once we're through.

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:02.680
Who are you?

00:02:16.070 --> 00:02:18.400
We're currently located at 34 Wainton Street.

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:20.530
We suspect foul play, and we also have a car.

00:02:20.530 --> 00:02:23.240
License number: FN34NOK

00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:24.540
Please confirm the owner.

00:02:26.870 --> 00:02:32.540
According to her personal effects, the female homicide is Eleanor Szabo, age 31.

00:02:32.540 --> 00:02:34.500
She's a Romanian national.

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:39.220
But since she was likely engaging in perfidy, it's highly possible that she is using a fake name.

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:43.510
This man here is Valeri Bilozerchev

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:46.430
He's a diplomat serving the Russian embassy.

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:50.520
So they were both shot once in the forehead and in the heart?

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:52.900
We're not talking about any petty criminal here.

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:54.150
No doubt.

00:02:55.070 --> 00:02:56.360
Witnesses?

00:02:56.360 --> 00:02:57.820
Right now there are none.

00:02:57.820 --> 00:03:01.070
If you find one, make sure they're put in police custody.

00:03:01.070 --> 00:03:03.410
They're lives might be in jeopardy.

00:03:03.410 --> 00:03:04.240
Affirmative.

00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:10.540
We've received a call from the Russian embassy.

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:13.500
They've confirmed that he is indeed Mr. Bilozerchev, their diplomat.

00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:17.510
They will also be the ones who will inform his family.

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:20.050
That's a weight off my shoulders.

00:03:20.050 --> 00:03:26.970
I'd never be able to tell the surviving family members that he was shot during a sexual liaison with his lover.

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:32.900
I walk unsteadily on paths to nowhere

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:33.350
Doutei Subs Presents:

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:37.020
wondering what I should do right now.

00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:43.490
I play the song you like on the car stereo

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:48.040
with the volume up and my feelings crystallized

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:53.670
driving on streets with no crossroads or signals

00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:59.090
with a speed that will catch up with you.

00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:03.550
So faraway - let's run!

00:04:03.890 --> 00:04:09.850
And let's not bother with the breaks - full throttle.

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:14.150
Oh someday - one of these days

00:04:14.350 --> 00:04:19.230
You'll be at my place where nobody can find you.

00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:25.320
Whenever you suffer a breakdown one can't see

00:04:25.570 --> 00:04:30.910
depend on me for your repairs.

00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:35.290
So faraway - let's run!

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:41.510
We'll reset and start again - even at our limit.

00:04:41.710 --> 00:04:45.800
Oh someday - one of these days

00:04:46.010 --> 00:04:51.850
If I'm with you we'll find our dream.

00:04:57.150 --> 00:05:02.070
Night Fog in Petticoat Lane

00:04:58.480 --> 00:05:02.320
This is aquatic patrol. Right now we have nothing in particular to report, over.

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:03.740
HQ here, copy that.

00:05:04.490 --> 00:05:08.570
Route 3, checkpoint 2. Currently all quiet.

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:10.080
Copy.

00:05:11.120 --> 00:05:13.410
Route 1, checkpoint 7.

00:05:13.410 --> 00:05:17.120
We have two men in custody for marijuana possession, but they appear to be unrelated to the case.

00:05:21.590 --> 00:05:23.050
What's going on?

00:05:23.050 --> 00:05:25.970
Probably just another murder or robbery.

00:05:25.970 --> 00:05:28.970
But they've set up checkpoints all over the place.

00:05:28.970 --> 00:05:32.100
I swear, it's such a bloody nuisance!

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:36.140
Hey, handsome!

00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:39.150
Why don't we party together? I'll make it worth your while!

00:05:39.150 --> 00:05:42.730
I'm the best lay in all Petticoat Lane you know...

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:46.150
Huh! Miserly knob!

00:05:54.040 --> 00:05:55.250
Here you are.

00:06:07.430 --> 00:06:09.970
Watch, I'll lay waste to these!

00:06:19.190 --> 00:06:21.020
Looks like there's no luck for you tonight, mate.

00:06:21.020 --> 00:06:23.400
Only because you can't rack 'em up.

00:06:24.070 --> 00:06:25.860
Now don't pout.

00:06:46.510 --> 00:06:47.470
Hmm?

00:06:48.800 --> 00:06:51.890
Bollocks, this table is crooked!

00:06:51.890 --> 00:06:53.970
Nah, it's just you.

00:06:54.470 --> 00:06:56.220
What will you have?

00:06:56.680 --> 00:06:59.560
Oh, may I have a beer?

00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:04.440
I'm sorry!

00:07:04.900 --> 00:07:06.780
Oi, keep the game moving!

00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:14.950
Shit!

00:07:16.330 --> 00:07:17.830
Don't fuss over him.

00:07:18.580 --> 00:07:22.670
A real player doesn't blame other people for his mistakes.

00:07:22.670 --> 00:07:24.460
Shut up, you old tosser!

00:07:25.750 --> 00:07:27.460
The barkeep is right!

00:07:30.090 --> 00:07:33.840
Hello? Do my eyes spy a foxy babe?

00:07:33.840 --> 00:07:38.770
And you're here at the counter drinking by yourself. Been having a rough time of it, love?

00:07:39.430 --> 00:07:42.270
Hey barkeep, take a look at this jukebox!

00:07:42.270 --> 00:07:44.440
I put in the money but it's refusing to play!

00:07:45.060 --> 00:07:47.860
You two better not pinch the bar money.

00:07:49.360 --> 00:07:52.320
When have we every stole any money?

00:07:52.320 --> 00:07:55.700
Don't I always bring in new customers for you?

00:07:55.700 --> 00:07:58.240
Yeah, and they're always ill-bred blokes.

00:07:58.660 --> 00:08:02.960
So babe, why don't we leave this dive and go dance or something?

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:05.290
I'm sorry.

00:08:05.290 --> 00:08:07.290
I don't feel up for that.

00:08:07.290 --> 00:08:10.090
All right, how about my apartment then?

00:08:10.670 --> 00:08:12.630
We'll show you a good time.

00:08:17.560 --> 00:08:18.680
What are...?

00:08:18.680 --> 00:08:21.560
You can see what I'm packing with your naked eyes, huh?

00:08:22.770 --> 00:08:24.770
Let me go!

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:30.280
Whoa now! Why have so much hate in you, babe?

00:08:29.150 --> 00:08:30.280
Will blighters lay off?

00:08:30.990 --> 00:08:35.660
If you wanna prove how macho you are, do it with the girl you screw on the side!

00:08:37.120 --> 00:08:38.450
Wrinkled old pisser!

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:47.380
You're not from around here, aren't you?

00:08:47.380 --> 00:08:48.380
Mm-hmm.

00:08:48.380 --> 00:08:53.170
A respectable London girl wouldn't be out around here alone.

00:09:25.160 --> 00:09:26.870
Are you on a trip here?

00:09:26.870 --> 00:09:29.130
We're from the London Metropolitan Police.

00:09:29.130 --> 00:09:31.500
Can we see your passport?

00:09:36.220 --> 00:09:38.840
Tougou Tadashi, Nationality: Japanese.

00:09:38.840 --> 00:09:41.060
So you're here on business?

00:09:41.060 --> 00:09:41.720
Correct.

00:09:42.310 --> 00:09:44.020
What type of work do you do?

00:09:44.020 --> 00:09:45.230
Sales.

00:09:47.980 --> 00:09:49.980
Thanks for your cooperation.

00:09:50.520 --> 00:09:53.320
There are a lot of bad sorts in this neighborhood.

00:09:53.320 --> 00:09:58.610
We advise you to return to your hotel before you get into some troubles.

00:09:58.610 --> 00:10:00.950
What is this about, Detective?

00:10:00.950 --> 00:10:05.000
Nobody comes to my bar to deal in drugs.

00:10:05.410 --> 00:10:08.000
We're not concerned with the petty hoodlums around here.

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:09.210
Meaning?

00:10:09.210 --> 00:10:13.300
About an hour ago, a Russian diplomat was murdered.

00:10:13.300 --> 00:10:17.010
And you're saying that the culprit ran off here to Petticoat Lane?

00:10:17.470 --> 00:10:19.390
We can't neither confirm nor deny.

00:10:19.390 --> 00:10:24.470
But the best way to avoid our cordons would be by sneaking off downtown.

00:10:25.020 --> 00:10:26.770
So there you have it.

00:10:26.770 --> 00:10:28.810
If something happens, let us know.

00:10:28.810 --> 00:10:31.060
Mm-hmm, got it.

00:10:38.110 --> 00:10:39.950
So they say it's a murder.

00:10:39.950 --> 00:10:43.830
So that's why I have to put up with all those cop-car sirens tonight.

00:10:47.200 --> 00:10:48.750
Stay safe!

00:11:08.430 --> 00:11:10.140
Please, wait!

00:11:14.860 --> 00:11:16.280
Buy me, please.

00:11:16.900 --> 00:11:20.910
Why are you selling your body if you're not a working girl?

00:11:22.570 --> 00:11:25.330
Must I explain myself?

00:12:12.960 --> 00:12:13.920
A robbery?

00:12:17.040 --> 00:12:19.880
No. A robber wouldn't shoot at us immediately.

00:12:27.140 --> 00:12:29.180
So will you buy me?

00:13:13.480 --> 00:13:18.110
I didn't want you to buy this body.

00:13:18.110 --> 00:13:22.030
I wanted you to buy this ridiculous "woman's ideal world" that I'm in.

00:13:22.030 --> 00:13:24.240
I hate what I've become.

00:13:24.820 --> 00:13:28.280
You can consider it as a stupid vacationer's caprice.

00:13:33.830 --> 00:13:37.420
But... I wonder why I chose you.

00:13:43.340 --> 00:13:44.880
Maybe...

00:13:44.880 --> 00:13:51.010
I see a light in your eyes that's emotionless and disconnected from reality.

00:14:05.780 --> 00:14:09.110
I saw them enter the hotel myself.

00:14:10.160 --> 00:14:12.080
Keep the engine running.

00:14:14.040 --> 00:14:17.080
Oh yes, I wonder how that actress is faring after-

00:14:19.630 --> 00:14:23.420
Unless you have a reservation, I'm afraid all the rooms are booked-

00:14:23.420 --> 00:14:24.130
Don't make noise.

00:14:24.550 --> 00:14:29.050
We aren't robbers. Just be quiet and do as we say.

00:14:30.050 --> 00:14:32.220
Say, can I ask you something?

00:14:32.220 --> 00:14:35.270
Why did you protect me earlier?

00:14:35.270 --> 00:14:41.060
You didn't even think about helping me when I was accosted by those two men at the bar.

00:15:08.670 --> 00:15:11.430
You kept a gun hidden in the bed?

00:15:12.430 --> 00:15:15.600
It was the one held by a man I killed earlier.

00:15:16.560 --> 00:15:18.230
Hurry and dress up.

00:15:18.230 --> 00:15:20.020
It's best we leave now.

00:15:28.530 --> 00:15:29.950
Let's leave from the back.

00:15:47.840 --> 00:15:48.880
We've spotted the target!

00:15:48.880 --> 00:15:50.420
What happened at the west side of the hotel?

00:16:10.530 --> 00:16:13.860
If we go in here, we'll be sitting ducks.

00:16:13.860 --> 00:16:16.120
You go find another entrance!

00:16:16.120 --> 00:16:17.200
Okay.

00:17:16.340 --> 00:17:18.350
Now it's my turn to ask.

00:17:20.060 --> 00:17:21.810
About your true identity.

00:17:23.640 --> 00:17:24.480
Oh?

00:17:25.520 --> 00:17:27.520
So you already knew.

00:17:28.520 --> 00:17:32.780
That I'm the same type of person as you.

00:17:33.860 --> 00:17:39.120
Two wolves can sense each other amidst a pack of dogs.

00:17:39.120 --> 00:17:41.910
Especially if they're male and female.

00:17:43.120 --> 00:17:47.790
When I saw you in the bar, I had an inkling you were no ordinary man.

00:17:48.670 --> 00:17:56.630
It wasn't long before I figured out that you were this key individual I saw at the CIA offices.

00:17:56.630 --> 00:17:59.050
The man called Golgo 13.

00:18:00.260 --> 00:18:02.760
Since you have so many enemies,

00:18:02.760 --> 00:18:08.810
I assumed that you'll mistake my pursuers as your own and repel their attacks.

00:18:09.980 --> 00:18:14.400
I'm CIA. Codename: Red Pepper.

00:18:15.780 --> 00:18:17.900
The incident with the diplomat?

00:18:18.490 --> 00:18:19.450
Me?

00:18:42.470 --> 00:18:43.220
Who are you?

00:18:55.110 --> 00:18:56.070
That's right.

00:18:56.070 --> 00:19:04.450
The men who came after us at the bar, and who came barging in at the hotel, they weren't after you.

00:19:04.450 --> 00:19:07.000
Their job was to eliminate me.

00:19:12.040 --> 00:19:18.380
I played my cards right and hired the world's top-ranked pro for free.

00:19:27.270 --> 00:19:28.390
I'm sorry.

00:19:29.230 --> 00:19:31.730
I'm not supposed to let anybody know.

00:19:32.190 --> 00:19:33.730
I get that a lot.

00:19:35.270 --> 00:19:39.150
If it's possible, I hope to have a peaceful separation.

00:19:56.380 --> 00:19:57.090
Shit!

00:20:33.120 --> 00:20:35.130
That was quite a blast.

00:20:35.630 --> 00:20:39.380
I'm just another woman when I'm with you.

00:20:39.380 --> 00:20:41.090
When did you realize that I wasn't?

00:20:43.970 --> 00:20:47.600
In any case, I want you to pretend you never noticed.

00:20:50.850 --> 00:20:54.020
Goodbye... Golgo 13.

00:21:27.720 --> 00:21:31.770
It's... not that I couldn't pull the trigger...

00:21:31.770 --> 00:21:34.480
...because I just shared a bed with you.

00:21:35.140 --> 00:21:36.900
I simply...

00:21:36.900 --> 00:21:38.900
...used up all my bullets.

00:21:42.530 --> 00:21:43.990
What if...

00:21:43.990 --> 00:21:46.490
...if I didn't point my gun at you?

00:21:47.490 --> 00:21:49.570
Would you have forgiven me?

00:22:00.790 --> 00:22:04.210
<i>Goodbye... my dear.</i>

00:22:44.000 --> 00:22:47.300
I  was worried with no one to talk to.

00:22:47.300 --> 00:22:50.340
I was brooding and standing still

00:22:50.340 --> 00:22:52.510
without moving a muscle.

00:22:53.180 --> 00:22:55.680
I wonder when that was?

00:22:56.180 --> 00:22:57.390
I'm sure

00:22:57.390 --> 00:23:00.560
you agonized over how

00:23:00.560 --> 00:23:05.820
people will hurt themselves and other people

00:23:06.440 --> 00:23:09.070
and fail to realize it.

00:23:09.450 --> 00:23:10.200
When

00:23:10.200 --> 00:23:13.620
the same days keep repeating themselves

00:23:13.620 --> 00:23:15.870
you never change.

00:23:16.580 --> 00:23:18.120
Since you're here for me

00:23:18.120 --> 00:23:22.420
I will accept the way that I am.

00:23:23.130 --> 00:23:26.670
I will never leave you alone

00:23:26.670 --> 00:23:30.010
I will softly touch your trembling heart.

00:23:30.220 --> 00:23:36.890
I realized that I'm not the only one who's alone.

00:23:36.890 --> 00:23:40.060
We're enveloped in the gentle sun beams.

00:23:40.060 --> 00:23:43.400
The long winter is finally over.

00:23:43.400 --> 00:23:50.030
The parts of us that were lonely will surely get stronger.

00:24:02.210 --> 00:24:05.340
A shot rang out over the snowy mountains.

00:24:05.340 --> 00:24:09.710
Golgo shot two moose with just one round.

00:24:09.710 --> 00:24:15.010
He was placed under arrest by the police for a hunting violation, just as he anticipated.

00:24:15.680 --> 00:24:20.850
That's because Golgo has come there to assassinate a certain character.

00:24:20.480 --> 00:24:26.270
On Large Mouth Lake

00:24:20.850 --> 00:24:25.310
Next time on Golgo 13: On Large Mouth Lake.

00:24:25.310 --> 00:24:28.820
Don't stand behind him, if you value your life.
